sc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5289a6353d07b40dfaad5f421c3d49793e9f3d0c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5289a6353d07b40dfaad5f421c3d49793e9f3d0c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 5:59PM MDT until October 22 at 10:15PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"Heavy rainfall is causing flooding along the South Fork of the Rio\nGrande, which is forecast to crest at 9.2 feet around 1 AM tonight.\nIf you live near the South Fork of the Rio Grande, and the main stem\nof the Rio Grande, take precautions to protect life and property from\nflooding.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Saguache, Central Mineral and Western Rio\nGrande Counties...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1015 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Several\nstructures are flooded and some sand bagging operations are\ncontinuing. Streams continue to rise due to excess runoff from\ncontinued rainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 552 PM MDT, South Fork Fire and Colorado State Patrol report\ncontinued rainfall across the warned area.\n- Water is currently near Highway 160 at Wolf Creek Ranch at mile\nmarker 177.  Several homes are also being flooded in the South\nFork area.  The river gauge on the south fork of the Rio Grande\n(SRGC2) is rapidly rising, and forecast to crest at 9.2 feet by 1\nAM tonight, and slowly fall during the overnight hours.  The main\nstem of the Rio Grande will likely run high down toward Del\nNorte.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDel Norte, South Fork, Wagon Wheel Gap, Wolf Creek Pass and\nCreede.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-22T22:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO; Saguache, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3d025e343077c60bfd8f01d7a0415054feb8704b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3d025e343077c60bfd8f01d7a0415054feb8704b.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 2:13PM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Ample sub-tropcial moisture will bring periods of moderate to\nheavy rain across the area from tonight into Friday morning\nbefore winding down Friday afternoon.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d926dc6d652870f5f8b98ab69b684b84f5ef12b5.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d926dc6d652870f5f8b98ab69b684b84f5ef12b5.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-22T23:54:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 222354 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 554 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flood Watch remains through the day Friday for the eastern San Juan mountains and the Upper Rio Grande Valley, with areal stream/river flooding and rock/mud slides possible. - Periods of moderate to heavy rain for the Continental Divide, tonight into early Friday,","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-22T06:48:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 220648 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1248 AM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 COZ058>